Description: Check whether a fence is signalled with its mutex held in llvmpipe.
 lp_fence_signal() increments the fence's count with the fence's mutex held, and then broadcasts its condition
 variable and unlocks the mutex. lp_fence_signalled() read the count without the mutex, so it could report the fence
 signalled while the last rasterizer thread was still between the increment and mtx_unlock(). Callers drop their
 reference once the fence is signalled, for example lp_setup_get_empty_scene() through lp_scene_end_rasterization(),
 and when that reference is the last one, lp_fence_destroy() frees the fence. The rasterizer thread then broadcasts the
 condition variable and unlocks the mutex in freed memory, and glibc's pthread_mutex_unlock() writes zero over the
 mutex's owner and decrements its user count, which corrupts an object the allocator has meanwhile placed in that
 memory. lp_fence_signalled() now reads the count with the mutex held, which orders the check after the unlock of the
 last signalling thread.
Author: Mitar <mitar.git@tnode.com>
Forwarded: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/46712
Last-Update: 2026-11-25
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/llvmpipe/lp_fence.c b/src/gallium/drivers/llvmpipe/lp_fence.c
index 4377750..6bbbada 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/llvmpipe/lp_fence.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/llvmpipe/lp_fence.c
@@ -176,8 +176,18 @@ lp_fence_signal(struct lp_fence *fence)
 bool
 lp_fence_signalled(struct lp_fence *f)
 {
-   if (f->type == LP_FENCE_TYPE_SW)
-      return f->count == f->rank;
+   if (f->type == LP_FENCE_TYPE_SW) {
+      /* The last rasterizer thread increments count with the mutex held, and
+       * still uses the mutex and the condition variable until it unlocks the
+       * mutex. Reading count with the mutex held orders this check after that
+       * unlock, so that a caller which releases the fence once it is signalled
+       * does not free it while that thread is still in lp_fence_signal().
+       */
+      mtx_lock(&f->mutex);
+      const bool signalled = f->count == f->rank;
+      mtx_unlock(&f->mutex);
+      return signalled;
+   }
 #ifdef HAVE_LIBDRM
    else {
       return sync_wait(f->sync_fd, 0) == 0;
